<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philips</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Royal Philips</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philips is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> multinational company founded in Eindhoven in 1891 by Gerard Philips and his father Frederik to make incandescent light bulbs. It grew into one of the world's largest electronics firms, making radios, televisions, audio cassettes and compact discs, and turned Eindhoven into an industrial city. It now concentrates on health technology and is headquartered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philips.jpg" alt="Philips" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ceescamel · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Prinses_Irenestraat_59,_Asd_(D).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
